// 003 - Key Vault secret reads with caller identity
// Purpose: see which identity read which secret, when, and whether it was allowed
// Data source: AzureDiagnostics (Key Vault audit logs via diagnostic setting diag-kv-to-sentinel)
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1552 Unsecured Credentials (unexpected reads / Forbidden attempts)
// Note: identity_claim_xms_mirid_s shows the resource that owns a managed identity
// Note: first logs from a new diagnostic setting can take 30-60 minutes to arrive
// Finding (lab): a Forbidden SecretGet = an identity asking for a secret it has no role on
// False positives: scheduled jobs reading their own secrets; compare against known identities
AzureDiagnostics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.KEYVAULT"
| where OperationName == "SecretGet"
| project TimeGenerated, ResultSignature, CallerIPAddress, id_s, identity_claim_xms_mirid_s
